# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Snickylink Launch project.

## Project Context
This is a vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript project without a build system or framework. The project structure includes:
- index.html (main HTML file)
- app.js (JavaScript functionality)
- styles.css (styling)
- assets/ (images and resources)

## Implementation Details

### What Was Done
Added Vercel Web Analytics to the project using the CDN-based approach recommended for vanilla HTML/JavaScript projects.

### Files Modified
- **index.html**: Added Vercel Analytics script tags in the `<head>` section

### Changes Made
Added two script tags before the closing `</head>` tag:

1. **Analytics initialization script**: Sets up the `window.va` global function that queues analytics events
2. **Analytics CDN script**: Loads the Vercel Analytics tracking script from `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js` with the `defer` attribute for optimal performance

### Why This Approach
According to the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart and https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package):

- For vanilla HTML/JavaScript projects without build tools, the CDN-based approach is recommended
- The npm package `@vercel/analytics` is intended for projects with module bundlers
- The CDN script automatically handles pageview tracking without additional configuration
- The `defer` attribute ensures the script loads asynchronously without blocking page rendering

### Next Steps
To enable analytics data collection:

1. **Enable Web Analytics** in your Vercel project dashboard (Settings > Analytics)
2. **Deploy the project** to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. **Verify setup** by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*` routes

### Notes
- No package.json or dependencies were needed since this is a static HTML project
- The analytics will automatically start tracking pageviews once deployed to Vercel
- The implementation preserves all existing code structure and functionality
- The script uses the `defer` attribute to prevent blocking the page load
